Bridge: keep the host's default route address when filtering Docker-like IPs.

go2rtc's WebRTC API drops every local IPv4 address in 172.16.0.0/12, which it
treats as Docker. An iPhone personal hotspot hands out 172.20.10.x, inside that
range, so on a Mac tethered to a phone the only routed address was dropped: STUN
and TURN went out through an unrouted interface (Docker Desktop's bridge100), no
reflexive or relay candidate was gathered, and the camera hung up after 15 s
(disconnect, close_reason 100). The filter now keeps the address of the default
route and still drops the rest of the range.

Applied by Scripts/build-core.sh to a copy of Vendor/aventproxy/avent-webrtc-bridge.

